{"id":"35b4e1443f7ccdbf","group":"14","path":"14/14-df-kan-extensions.md","title":"Definition — Kan Extensions (supplement)","display":"Definition — Kan Extensions (supplement)","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Sheaves in Geometry and Logic (Mac Lane & Moerdijk)","book_abbrev":"14","label":"14-df-kan-extensions","aliases":["14-df-kan-extensions"],"display":"Definition — Kan Extensions (supplement)","depends_on":["[[14-df-functor]]","[[14-df-natural-transformation]]","[[14-df-identity-composite-functors]]","[[14-df-natural-transformation-composition-whiskering]]"],"source_status":"来源定位沿用附件笔记；本次未重新核验原书文件。"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Sheaves in Geometry and Logic (Mac Lane &amp; Moerdijk)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"14"},{"key":"label","html":"14-df-kan-extensions"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>14-df-kan-extensions</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Definition — Kan Extensions (supplement)"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1f1269584b34ad4b\" href=\"?note=1f1269584b34ad4b\" title=\"14-df-functor\">14-df-functor</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1bdaf4a293143165\" href=\"?note=1bdaf4a293143165\" title=\"14-df-natural-transformation\">14-df-natural-transformation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"dad26c5de724390a\" href=\"?note=dad26c5de724390a\" title=\"14-df-identity-composite-functors\">14-df-identity-composite-functors</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f012515fd4cf0061\" href=\"?note=f012515fd4cf0061\" title=\"14-df-natural-transformation-composition-whiskering\">14-df-natural-transformation-composition-whiskering</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_status","html":"来源定位沿用附件笔记；本次未重新核验原书文件。"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(F,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal E),\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(K,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\">\\(\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(F,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal E),\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(K,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\)</span> (functors, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"1f1269584b34ad4b\" href=\"?note=1f1269584b34ad4b\" title=\"14-df-functor\">14-df-functor</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IsNatural}\">\\(\\mathrm{IsNatural}\\)</span> (natural-transformation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"1bdaf4a293143165\" href=\"?note=1bdaf4a293143165\" title=\"14-df-natural-transformation\">14-df-natural-transformation</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IsLan},\\mathrm{IsRan}\">\\(\\mathrm{IsLan},\\mathrm{IsRan}\\)</span> (Kan-extension predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\Bigl(\\mathrm{IsLan}(L,\\eta,F,K)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(L,\\mathcal D,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\eta,F,L\\circ K)\\land\\forall M\\;(\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(M,\\mathcal D,\\mathcal E)\\to\\forall\\alpha\\;(\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\alpha,F,M\\circ K)\\to\\exists!\\beta\\;(\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\beta,L,M)\\land(\\beta K)\\circ\\eta=\\alpha)))\\Bigr)\\land\\Bigl(\\mathrm{IsRan}(R,\\varepsilon,F,K)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(R,\\mathcal D,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\varepsilon,R\\circ K,F)\\land\\forall M\\;(\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(M,\\mathcal D,\\mathcal E)\\to\\forall\\alpha\\;(\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\alpha,M\\circ K,F)\\to\\exists!\\beta\\;(\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\beta,M,R)\\land\\varepsilon\\circ(\\beta K)=\\alpha)))\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\Bigl(\\mathrm{IsLan}(L,\\eta,F,K)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(L,\\mathcal D,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\eta,F,L\\circ K)\\land\\forall M\\;(\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(M,\\mathcal D,\\mathcal E)\\to\\forall\\alpha\\;(\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\alpha,F,M\\circ K)\\to\\exists!\\beta\\;(\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\beta,L,M)\\land(\\beta K)\\circ\\eta=\\alpha)))\\Bigr)\\land\\Bigl(\\mathrm{IsRan}(R,\\varepsilon,F,K)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(R,\\mathcal D,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\varepsilon,R\\circ K,F)\\land\\forall M\\;(\\mathrm{IsFunctor}(M,\\mathcal D,\\mathcal E)\\to\\forall\\alpha\\;(\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\alpha,M\\circ K,F)\\to\\exists!\\beta\\;(\\mathrm{IsNatural}(\\beta,M,R)\\land\\varepsilon\\circ(\\beta K)=\\alpha)))\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书定位：VII.5 Points（印刷页 380 附近）、VII 练习 3；原书将定义指向 CWM。</p>\n<p>这是对原书出现的 Kan 延拓术语作的内部辅助展开，并非原书 II.6 定义。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\beta K\">\\(\\beta K\\)</span> 表示右 whiskering，垂直复合与该记号在 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"f012515fd4cf0061\" href=\"?note=f012515fd4cf0061\" title=\"14-df-natural-transformation-composition-whiskering\">14-df-natural-transformation-composition-whiskering</a> 定义。左右普遍性质分别是在相应逗号范畴中的始对象和终对象。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"14-df-functor","status":"resolved","id":"1f1269584b34ad4b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[14-df-functor]]","embed":false},{"target":"14-df-natural-transformation","status":"resolved","id":"1bdaf4a293143165","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[14-df-natural-transformation]]","embed":false},{"target":"14-df-identity-composite-functors","status":"resolved","id":"dad26c5de724390a","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[14-df-identity-composite-functors]]","embed":false},{"ta